"Return a title (https://help.audible.com/s/article/return-a-title)\nciteturn762view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/return-a-title\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 120\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Account Ask A Question Membership Plans & benefits+2\nL13: ## Return a title\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Return a title\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: return-a-title\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: \nL29: \nL30: Remember, you cannot return titles directly from the Audible app. You must use the website to initiate the return process.\nL31: As long as they meet the eligibility requirements, 【1†Audible Premium】 members have the option to return audiobooks and get their credit back. This option lets you return titles purchased in error or explore different narrators and stories risk-free. You can return an audiobook through the Audible website.\nL32: \nL33: In this article:\nL34:   * 【2†Eligibility requirements】\nL35:   * 【3†How do I return an audiobook on mobile?】\nL36:   * 【4†How do I return an audiobook on desktop?】\nL37:   * 【5†What happens to your Audible title when you return its companion Kindle eBook?】\nL38: ## Eligibility requirements\nL39: \nL40:   * You must be an active 【1†Audible Premium】 member in good standing.\nL41:   * You're making the return within 365 days of its purchase date.\nL42:   * You purchased the title with an Audible credit.\nL43: Note: We reserve the right to limit the number of returns or revoke return privileges at our discretion. Based on your return history, the self-service refund option may not be available. Audible may cancel or modify the terms of our returns option with respect to any or all participants at any time. Customers who cancel or fail to maintain their membership in good standing are not eligible to make returns. This return option doesn't affect any rights you have under consumer law.\nL44: Returns may only be made through the same method in which you purchased the title. For example, if you purchased a title through the Google Play Store or App Store, you can only return that title through the Google Play Store or App Store customer service.\nL45: ## How do I return an audiobook on mobile?\nL46: \nL47: Return Audible titles from your iOS device or Android device by following these steps:\nL48: \nL49:   1. Go to 【6†www.audible.com†www.audible.com】 and sign in to your account.\nL50:   2. Select the main menu.\nL51:   3. Select your name.\nL52:   4. Select 【7†Purchase history†www.audible.com】.\nL53:   5. Find the title you want to return and select it.\nL54:   6. Select Return this title and confirm.\nL55: Note: Refunded 【8†credits】 will expire 12 months after being issued, regardless of the original credit type. After confirming your return, 1 credit will be added back to your account.\nL56: ## How do I return an audiobook on desktop?\nL57: \nL58:   1. Select your username from the site's top navigation or select 【9†Membership Details†www.audible.com】.\nL59:   2. Select 【7†Purchase history†www.audible.com】.\nL60:   3. Next to the title you want to return, select Return this title.\nL61:   4. Confirm the return.\nL62: \nL63: Note: Refunded 【8†credits】 will expire 12 months after being issued, regardless of the original credit type. After confirming your return, 1 credit will be added back to your account.\nL64: ## What happens to your Audible title when you return its companion Kindle eBook?\nL65: When you purchase an Audible title at a discounted price through the \"Add Narration\" offer (which offers savings when you purchase an audiobook alongside its Kindle eBook), the two titles are linked. If you later make an eligible return of that Kindle eBook, Audible will automatically process a refund for the Audible title and remove it from your Library. This refund will be issued to your original payment method, and you will receive a notification when this action occurs.\nL66: \nL67: Did this answer your question?\nL68: 【10†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL69: \nL70: \nL71: \nL72: 【11†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL73: \nL74:  Back to top\nL75: \nL76: 【12†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL77: \nL78: 【13†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL79: ## Need more assistance?\nL80: \nL81: Chat now【14†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL82: \nL83: \nL84: \nL85: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL86: \nL87: \nL88: \nL89: Worst\nL90: \nL91: 1\nL92: \nL93: 2\nL94: \nL95: 3\nL96: \nL97: 4\nL98: \nL99: 5\nL100: \nL101: 6\nL102: \nL103: 7\nL104: \nL105: Best\nL106: \nL107: \nL108: \nL109: Region\nL110: \nL111: United States\nL112: \nL113: Language\nL114: \nL115: English\nL116: \nL117: Loading\nL118: \nL119: Return a title 【15†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAudio quality issues (https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-won-t-play-has-poor-audio-quality)\nciteturn762view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-won-t-play-has-poor-audio-quality\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 276\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Alexa Ask A Question Fire TV iOS Kindle+3\nL13: ## Audio quality issues\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Audio quality issues\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: title-won-t-play-has-poor-audio-quality\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: In this article, you'll find troubleshooting steps for general playback issues by device type.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31: \nL32:   * 【1†Playback issues in the app】\nL33:   * 【2†Playback issues on your Samsung or Pixel device】\nL34:   * 【3†How to fix playback issues on Alexa】\nL35:   * 【4†Playback issues on Fire Tablet】\nL36:   * 【5†Playback issues on Fire TV】\nL37:   * 【6†Playback issues on Cloud Player】\nL38: ## Playback issues in the app\nL39: \nL40: Update app\nL41: \nL42: If your title won't play, you may have to update your Audible app.\nL43: \nL44: To update the Audible app on iOS:\nL45: \nL46:   1. Open the App Store.\nL47:   2. Select your profile icon.\nL48:   3. Find and select the Audible app.\nL49:   4. Select Update.\nL50:   5. Select Open to view the latest version of the Audible app.\nL51: \nL52: Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\nL53: \nL54: To update the Audible app on Android:\nL55:   1. Open the Google Play Store.\nL56:   2. Select your profile icon.\nL57:   3. Select Manage apps & device.\nL58:   4. Find the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\nL59:   5. Select Update.\nL60: \nL61: Re-download your title\nL62: \nL63: If your title is skipping chapters or seems to have missing content, you might have an incomplete download or missing content.\nL64: \nL65: Step 1: Remove title from device\nL66: \nL67:   1. Go to your Library.\nL68:   2. Select your title's 3-dot menu.\nL69:   3. Select Remove download.\nL70: \nL71: Step 2: Re-download your title\nL72:   1. Go to your Library.\nL73:   2. Select your title to re-download.\nL74: \nL75: Note: Your title will pick up where you left off after you re-download it.\nL76: \nL77: Listen on another device\nL78: \nL79: If your title won't play at all, it's possible the issue may be with the device itself and not the Audible app. Try listening to the title using our Cloud Player or another Audible-ready device to see if the issue continues.\nL80:   1. Open the Audible website and sign in.\nL81:   2. From the Library on the site's navigation, select Audiobooks.\nL82:   3. Select Listen now or Play next to the title of your choosing.\nL83:   4. The Cloud Player will appear.\nL84: \nL85: Change download quality\nL86: \nL87: If your audio quality is poor or you hear static and background noises, changing the download quality may resolve your problem.\nL88:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL89:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL90:   3. Select Data & Storage.\nL91:   4. Choose between Standard or High.\nL92:   5. Select Library.\nL93:   6. Select the 3-dot menu next to your title.\nL94:   7. Select Remove download.\nL95:   8. Re-download the title to your Audible library.\nL96: ## Playback issues on your Samsung or Pixel device\nL97: \nL98: If your title won't play when you lock your screen, use another app, or use the timer, then the Android app might be set to \"Restricted\" in your device's battery settings.\nL99: \nL100: Update your Samsung battery settings\nL101: \nL102:   1. Open your device Settings.\nL103:   2. Select Apps.\nL104:   3. Select Audible.\nL105:   4. Select Battery.\nL106:   5. Choose from one of these available options:\nL107:   * Unrestricted: The Audible app will run in the background without any restriction and will continue playing your title until you stop it. This option may increase battery usage.\nL108:   * Optimised: Your device will learn how you use the app and will put the app to sleep based on your usage patterns. Your titles may still occasionally stop until the device learns how you use it.\nL109: \nL110: Update your Pixel battery settings\nL111: \nL112: Step 1: Turn on Adaptive battery\nL113:   1. Open your device Settings.\nL114:   2. Select Battery.\nL115:   3. Select Adaptive Preferences.\nL116:   4. Turn on Adaptive Battery.\nL117: \nL118: Note: When your battery is low, adaptive battery may reduce your device's performance.\nL119: \nL120: Step 2: Update your battery settings\nL121:   1. From Settings, select Apps.\nL122:   2. Select See all apps.\nL123:   3. Select the Audible app.\nL124:   4. Select Battery.\nL125:   5. Choose from one of these available options:\nL126:      * Unrestricted: The Audible app will run in the background without any restriction and will continue playing your title until you stop it. This option may increase battery usage.\nL127:      * Optimized: Your device will learn how you use the app and will put the app to sleep based on your usage patterns. Your titles may still occasionally stop until the device learns how you use it.\nL128: Note: If you start experiencing excessive battery drain when using the Audible app, please make sure you've updated to the app's latest version.\nL129: ## How to fix playback issues on Alexa\nL130:   * Make sure your device is turned on. There should be a blue light on top.\nL131:   * Make sure your device is connected to your Amazon account.\nL132:   * Check to see if your username for Audible is the same for Amazon. If not, combine your Amazon and Audible accounts and Alexa will play your titles.\nL133:   * Check your Alexa companion app's connection. If there's an error, it could mean your device is unplugged. Make sure it's plugged in and ask Alexa to play your title.\nL134:   * It's possible that your Amazon Family settings may be impacting your ability to hear certain titles. Visit the Manage My Family page on Amazon's website to ensure that your Amazon Family settings are correct.\nL135: Note: Teen profiles don't have access to titles in your Family Library. To remove a teen profile from your Amazon Family, please visit Amazon's Help Center.\nL136: ## Playback issues on Fire Tablet\nL137: \nL138: If you are experiencing playback issues on your Fire Tablet, please try the troubleshooting options below:\nL139: \nL140: Reboot the device\nL141: \nL142: You may need to turn your device off and on again.\nL143: \nL144:   1. Hold the Power button down for 30 seconds until the device turns off.\nL145:   2. Press the Power button to turn the device back on.\nL146: \nL147: Remove download and re-download the audiobook\nL148: \nL149: If you experience playback issues with a title, you may need to delete it and download it again.\nL150:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL151:   2. Select Library.\nL152:   3. Tap and hold down on the cover art of the corrupted audiobook to select.\nL153:   4. Once a checkmark appears in the middle of the title, tap Remove download.\nL154:   5. Once deleted, attempt to re-download.\nL155: \nL156: Change download quality\nL157: \nL158: One reason your title won't play is because of the download format. To change the format:\nL159:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL160:   2. Go to your Profile.\nL161:   3. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL162:   4. Select Data & Storage.\nL163:   5. Choose between Standard or High.\nL164:   6. Then delete the title you have downloaded, and re-download the title to your Audible library.\nL165: \nL166: Force stop the app\nL167: \nL168: If your title won't play at all, you may have to force stop your Audible app.\nL169:   1. Drag down from the top of the screen and tap the Settings gear icon followed by Apps & Games.\nL170:   2. Tap Manage All Applications followed by Audible Store.\nL171:   3. Tap Force Stop followed by OK.\nL172: \nL173: Update your device\nL174: \nL175:   1. Go to the Settings gear icon on your Tablet home page.\nL176:   2. Scroll down to Device Options.\nL177:   3. Select System Updates and select Update.\nL178: ## Playback issues on Fire TV\nL179: \nL180:   * Check your device's internet connection.\nL181:   * Make sure you're signed in to the correct account.\nL182:   * If your username for Audible isn't the same for Amazon, combine your Amazon and Audible accounts.\nL183:   * Go to your Purchase History page to check that the title you're trying to listen to has a date listed under the Purchased column.\nL184:   * If you use the Fire TV Remote app on your phone, make sure the app is updated to the latest version.\nL185: ## Playback issues on Cloud Player\nL186: \nL187: If you are experiencing playback issues, something could have happened with your saved browser history that is causing the Cloud Player to not pop up.\nL188: \nL189: First, make sure you have the latest version of your web browser. If the problem persists, follow the steps below.\nL190: \nL191: Clear your web history\nL192: \nL193: Google Chrome:\nL194:   1. Select the more options button in the corner of the browser, followed by More tools and Clear browsing data.\nL195:   2. Place a checkmark in the following boxes: Browsing history, Download history, Cookies and other site and plug-in data, Cached images and files, Hosted app data, Content licenses.\nL196:   3. Select the beginning of time from the drop down menu.\nL197:   4. Select Clear browsing data.\nL198: \nL199: Safari:\nL200:   1. Select History at the top of Safari, followed by Clear History.\nL201:   2. In the box that pops up, choose all history from the drop-down menu.\nL202:   3. Select Clear History.\nL203:   4. Go back to the Audible website, and attempt to play your audiobook again by selecting Play.\nL204: \nL205: Firefox:\nL206: \nL207:   1. Select the menu button in the corner of the browser, followed by History.\nL208:   2. Select Clear Recent History.\nL209:   3. Select all the check boxes and change the \"Time range to clear\" to Everything.\nL210:   4. Select Clear Now.\nL211: Enabling Auto-Play\nL212: \nL213: If you are using Safari, you may need to enable Auto-Play to resolve your playback issues.\nL214: \nL215: Safari:\nL216: \nL217:   1. Select Safari at the top of the Safari browser while on Audible.com.\nL218:   2. Select Settings for This Website.\nL219:   3. Select Allow All Auto-Play.\nL220: \nL221: Additionally, you can also press the Pause button after launching the Cloud Player to initiate playback.\nL222: \nL223: Did this answer your question?\nL224: \nL225: 【7†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL226: \nL227: \nL228: \nL229: 【8†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL230: \nL231:  Back to top\nL232: 【9†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL233: \nL234: 【10†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL235: ## Need more assistance?\nL236: \nL237: 【11†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL238: \nL239: \nL240: \nL241: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL242: \nL243: \nL244: \nL245: Worst\nL246: \nL247: 1\nL248: \nL249: 2\nL250: \nL251: 3\nL252: \nL253: 4\nL254: \nL255: 5\nL256: \nL257: 6\nL258: \nL259: 7\nL260: \nL261: Best\nL262: \nL263: \nL264: \nL265: Region\nL266: \nL267: United States\nL268: \nL269: Language\nL270: \nL271: English\nL272: \nL273: Loading\nL274: \nL275: Audio quality issues 【12†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about immersion reading (https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-immersion-reading)\nciteturn762view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn754view1\",\"id\":2}); Total lines: 123\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Accessibility Android iOS Kindle Listening Ways to listen\nL13: ## Learn about immersion reading\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 12, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Learn about immersion reading\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: learn-about-immersion-reading\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Immersion reading lets you read and listen to a book at the same time. The text highlights as the narrator reads, so you can follow along in the Kindle eBook while listening to the audiobook. This feature is available for titles that support 【1†Read & Listen】.\nL29: \nL30: Note: Immersion reading uses the professional narrator from your audiobook, not text-to-speech.\nL31: In this article:\nL32: \nL33:   * 【2†What is immersion reading?】\nL34:   * 【3†What do I need to use immersion reading?】\nL35:   * 【4†Which devices support immersion reading?】\nL36:   * 【5†How do I start immersion reading?】\nL37:   * 【6†How do I customize my reading experience?】\nL38: ## What is immersion reading?\nL39: \nL40: Immersion reading shows you the Kindle eBook text with words highlighted as the audiobook plays. It helps you follow along and stay focused while listening. You can see the text on your screen and hear the narrator at the same time.\nL41: ## What do I need to use immersion reading?\nL42: \nL43: To use immersion reading, you need:\nL44: \nL45:   * Both the 【1†Read & Listen】 supported versions of the audiobook and Kindle eBook for the same title.\nL46:   * An internet connection: the eBook text loads from the internet in the Audible app.\nL47: \nL48: Note: Some pages are saved so you can still see them without an internet connection.\nL49: ## Which devices support immersion reading?\nL50: \nL51: The following devices support immersion reading:\nL52: \nL53:   * Audible Mobile Apps (Android, iOS).\nL54:   * Fire Tablet FOS8 and above.\nL55:   * Audible Apps on iPad and Android Tablets.\nL56:   * Audible App for macOS.\nL57: ## How do I start immersion reading?\nL58: \nL59:   1. Open an audiobook with a 【1†Read & Listen】 badge in the Audible app.\nL60:   2. While playing a title, use the toggle above the cover image to switch from Listen to Read & Listen.\nL61:   3. Follow along with the highlighted text while you listen.\nL62: ## How do I customize my reading experience?\nL63: \nL64: You can change the following settings while using immersion reading:\nL65: \nL66:   * Font style: Choose a font that's easy for you to read.\nL67:   * Text size: Use the slider to make text bigger or smaller.\nL68:   * Theme: Switch between light or dark mode.\nL69:   * Playback speed: Speed up or slow down how fast the narrator reads.\nL70:   * Chapter navigation: Use the menu to jump between chapters.\nL71: \nL72: Did this answer your question?\nL73: \nL74: 【7†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL75: 【8†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL76: \nL77:  Back to top\nL78: \nL79: 【9†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL80: \nL81: 【10†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL82: ## Need more assistance?\nL83: \nL84: 【11†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL85: \nL86: \nL87: \nL88: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL89: \nL90: \nL91: \nL92: Worst\nL93: \nL94: 1\nL95: \nL96: 2\nL97: \nL98: 3\nL99: \nL100: 4\nL101: \nL102: 5\nL103: \nL104: 6\nL105: \nL106: 7\nL107: \nL108: Best\nL109: \nL110: \nL111: \nL112: Region\nL113: \nL114: United States\nL115: \nL116: Language\nL117: \nL118: English\nL119: \nL120: Loading\nL121: \nL122: Learn about immersion reading 【12†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHelp Center Desktop (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-collections)\nciteturn762view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn754view1\",\"id\":12}); Redirected to URL: https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-collections?language=en_US; Total lines: 7\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: CSS Error\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUse Page Sync (https://help.audible.com/s/article/use-page-sync)\nciteturn762view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn754view1\",\"id\":15}); Total lines: 130\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Library Listening\nL13: ## Use Page Sync\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Use Page Sync\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: use-page-sync\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Page Sync lets you seamlessly switch between reading your physical book and listening to the audiobook. With the corresponding audiobook open in the Audible app, simply scan a page with your phone's camera, and your audiobook automatically jumps to that exact spot—no manual searching needed.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†What is Page Sync?】\nL32:   * 【2†How do I use Page Sync?】\nL33:   * 【3†Which titles work with Page Sync?】\nL34:   * 【4†Troubleshooting】\nL35: ## What is Page Sync?\nL36: \nL37: Page Sync uses your phone's camera to recognize text from your physical book and automatically syncs your listening position in the audiobook to match where you are in your physical book.\nL38: \nL39: Note: Page Sync allows you to sync from the physical book to the audiobook, but not from the audiobook to the physical book. As audiobooks do not have page numbers, Page Sync cannot indicate the page number of the physical book.\nL40: ## How do I use Page Sync?\nL41: \nL42:   1. Open the audiobook in the Audible app that corresponds to the physical book you want to scan.\nL43:   2. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL44:   3. Select Page Sync.\nL45:   4. Grant camera permission (first-time only).\nL46:   5. Hold your camera over any page of text in your physical book.\nL47:   6. The app automatically captures and recognizes the text.\nL48:   7. Your audiobook jumps to the matching position.\nL49: \nL50: Note:\nL51:   * Keep the page flat and well-lit for best results.\nL52:   * Make sure the text is fully visible in your camera frame.\nL53:   * The app provides real-time feedback on text readability.\nL54: ## Which titles work with Page Sync?\nL55: \nL56: Page Sync is available for select English-language audiobooks. Your audiobook doesn't need to be downloaded to use this feature. You can access Page Sync from the 3-dot More menu.\nL57: \nL58: Not supported:\nL59: \nL60:   * Podcasts\nL61:   * Audible Originals without book equivalents\nL62:   * Kids Profiles\nL63:   * Children's picture books\nL64: \nL65: Note: Page Sync works with any edition of your physical book if the text matches the audiobook.\nL66: ## Troubleshooting\nL67: \nL68: If Page Sync isn't working:\nL69: \nL70:   * Check your internet connection (Page Sync requires an active internet connection).\nL71:   * Ensure camera permissions are enabled in your device settings.\nL72:   * Make sure the text is fully visible in your camera frame.\nL73:   * Improve lighting and keep the page flat.\nL74: \nL75: Note: Different book editions may have different page numbers. Page Sync works best when your physical book edition closely matches the audiobook version.\nL76: \nL77: Did this answer your question?\nL78: 【5†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL79: \nL80: \nL81: \nL82: 【6†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL83: \nL84:  Back to top\nL85: \nL86: 【7†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL87: \nL88: 【8†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL89: ## Need more assistance?\nL90: \nL91: 【9†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL92: \nL93: \nL94: \nL95: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL96: \nL97: \nL98: \nL99: Worst\nL100: \nL101: 1\nL102: \nL103: 2\nL104: \nL105: 3\nL106: \nL107: 4\nL108: \nL109: 5\nL110: \nL111: 6\nL112: \nL113: 7\nL114: \nL115: Best\nL116: \nL117: \nL118: \nL119: Region\nL120: \nL121: United States\nL122: \nL123: Language\nL124: \nL125: English\nL126: \nL127: Loading\nL128: \nL129: Use Page Sync 【10†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n"
